@flexiarg operator/name-the-phrase-you-did-not-follow
@title Say You Are Lost And Quote The Phrase That Lost You
@status accepted 2026-11-11: proposed by 象 for 2 turns (Joe 2026-11-11: recurrence suffices); attested once used in a mission or a War Machine cascade
@provenance 象 proposals, ~/.emacs-graph/session-turn-analysis/<record>[.json].candidates.json; records: turn-Tca03g turn-fD5qto; first proposed for: The agent has explained something with its own vocabulary.
@why [writing-coherence/plain-language-thesis]

! conclusion: quote the exact phrase that lost you, so the agent restates that part in plain words

  + IF:
    Joe cannot follow the explanation

  + HOWEVER:
    a bare 'I don't understand' gives the agent nothing to repair

  + THEN:
    quote the exact phrase that lost you, so the agent restates that part in plain words

  + BECAUSE:
    the quoted phrase locates the gap for a cheap repair
